dencies":[],"digest":"e3c81e90238fd31ac9aeb6e00518043e17647cc32f299c380bb1ee272a8aafe1"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":57728,"output_tokens":2820,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"e26efc950921c0dda688770459f0f6f871ca7fb1aa3d29f0f34fd0f608759065"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":144547,"output_tokens":5163,"requests":11}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how container-criterion children are rehydrated with faithful at-review `title`/`description` (the corpus persists only bare child ids) — e.g. reconstruct each child's material from history, or exclude container criteria from admission and document that scope.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'for a container criterion — the row's `children` (persisted as bare ticket-id strings) NORMALIZED into the `{ticket_id, title, description}` records the container finder requires before dispatch'","corpus.py `_child_ids` returns only `item['canonical_id']`; `_build_sidecar_row` stores `\"children\": children` (bare strings); even `_build_context` builds `children=[{\"ticket_id\": c} ...]` — no title/description persisted","eval_solver.py:129-137 passes children into `pass1_container`; container_stage.build_sibling_roster and passes.py:369-378 render each child's `title`/`description` — which will be empty after normalization","The reproduction premise ('current code still agrees with history') requires the finder to see the SAME material the original review saw; empty child title/description breaks that for container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape)"],"finding":"For container criteria, the rehydration cannot produce the `{ticket_id, title, description}` child records the container finder consumes: the corpus persists children only as bare ticket-id strings, so per-child `title`/`description` are unrecoverable — the finder then runs over children with empty content, making the reproduction verdict (admit vs. drift) unfaithful to the historical review.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f41073a9ac678ef31","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Rehydrate, then run' (container child normalization); vs. corpus.py:_build_sidecar_row/_child_ids and eval_solver.py:120-137 / passes.py container render","norm_id":"n312be2d3fb55c87c","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A must-fire container (decomp-shape) case whose finding depended on child descriptions no longer reproduces — wrongly routed to drift","A no_fire container case spuriously reproduces because the near-empty children can't trigger the criterion — admitting an unfaithful spec"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either extend the corpus sidecar row to persist per-child at-review `title`/`description` (reconstructed from each child ticket's history at review_ts, matching the fingerprint ladder) so container children rehydrate faithfully, or explicitly scope container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape) OUT of the admission runner until child material is capturable, and state that in Non-goals.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how container-criterion children are rehydrated with the `title` and `description` the finder consumes — either persist per-child title/description in the sidecar row or resolve them at rehydration — or scope container criteria out and state that the corpus supplies no per-child AC vocabulary.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the row’s `children` (persisted as bare ticket-id strings) NORMALIZED into the `{ticket_id, title, description}` records the container finder requires before dispatch.'","corpus.py:237-244 `_child_ids` returns a list of bare `canonical_id` STRINGS; `_build_sidecar_row` (corpus.py:270-288) stores exactly that list under `children` — no per-child title or description is persisted.","container_stage.py:77-94 `build_sibling_roster` reads `child.get('title','')` and parses each child's `description` for acceptance criteria; docstring: a title-only roster meant 'G3 could not fire on an uncovered parent criterion (bug creamy-cocksure-elkhound)'.","fixture_admission.py:309 the only realizable normalization is `{'ticket_id': c}` — title/description cannot be reconstructed from a bare id, and the plan names no source for them."],"finding":"The plan claims per-child records are normalized into `{ticket_id, title, description}` 'the container finder requires,' but the sidecar corpus persists children as bare ticket-id strings only (no title/description), so the container finder receives an impoverished roster and a container must-fire case can silently fail to reproduce.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f28f9951fad284574","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Rehydrate, then run'","norm_id":"n021122fd28ffe6af","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A container criterion (G3/G4/decomp-shape) must-fire case whose firing depends on sibling-coverage of an uncovered parent AC is replayed; the rehydrated roster has no titles/ACs, G3 stays silent in ≥2/3 runs, the case is judged non-reproducing and drifted — a false-negative that discards a valid fixture."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend `_build_sidecar_row`/`_child_ids` to persist per-child `{canonical_id, title, description}` from the reviewed material (mirroring `_build_context`), and rehydrate those into `{ticket_id, title, description}` records; if that material is unrecoverable for a container case, withhold it to drift as unrecoverable rather than running the finder against a degraded roster.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Subject: 'a `review_event_uuid` — the join key to the review sidecar' and rehydrates from the matched row `description`/`children`","Emitter: 'input is a deterministic, model-free provenance descriptor rendered from the row's stable fields (its criterion, direction, tier, sorted signals, and norm_id (fire) or review_event_uuid (no_fire) and rank)'","Subject acceptance: 'A must-fire case whose review_event_uuid resolves to a sidecar row runs the finder on that row's rehydrated description'"],"finding":"The subject plan describes rehydrating each candidate's finder input from a verified sidecar row keyed by `review_event_uuid` — using the row's `description` as plan text and `children` for container criteria. But the emitter prerequisite explicitly defines the candidate row's `input` as a deterministic, model-free provenance descriptor rendered from stable fields, and states the row carries no `description`, no `children`, and no plan prose. Crucially, the emitter's provenance `input` renders `norm_id` for the fire direction and `review_event_uuid` ONLY for the no_fire direction. The subject relies on `review_event_uuid` as the join key for ALL candidates (including must-fire cases, per acceptance criteria), yet the emitter does not guarantee `review_event_uuid` is present/usable in the emitted spec's fire-direction cases — the descriptor for fire cases uses `norm_id` instead.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd4dfb0bea33e5f6","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: Rehydrate, then run","norm_id":"n2dcebfcb409124c7","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the drift-report write semantics under resume (e.g. rebuild the report wholesale from all non-reproducing cases each run, or key entries by (criterion, case id) idempotently) so a re-derived criterion neither duplicates nor clobbers existing entries.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a non-reproducing one is withheld to a drift report at docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md'","'the drift report and admitted specs are the only files written'","resume: 'a criterion is done iff its stable run_id ... is in the ledger' — but drift-report is not gated by the ledger, and its idempotency across a re-derivation is not stated"],"finding":"The drift-report writer's write semantics under resume are unspecified: the ledger is the resume oracle for criterion done-ness (done iff run_id present), but a criterion re-derived on resume (crash between the two ordered writes) would re-produce its drift entries, and the plan never states whether docs/experiments/.../drift-report.md is rebuilt wholesale or appended — risking duplicated or clobbered entries.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5aa4634f6467df8a","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Disposition / Failure disposition sections","norm_id":"n964f43c8b80a539f","priority":0.066,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Crash between spec os.replace and ledger finalize; resume re-derives the criterion and re-emits drift entries into an already-partially-written report."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that the drift report is rebuilt in full from the current run's disposition (or keyed idempotently by (criterion, case_id, review_event_uuid)), independent of the ledger resume oracle, so re-derivation on resume is safe.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Subject uses cap_usd=250.0, reserve_usd=0.0 and estimate keys criteria-eval-cheap/criteria-eval-agent","Prerequisite adds those exact keys and keyword-only cap_usd/reserve_usd params"],"finding":"The subject calls `ledger.reserve(estimate_usd, ledger_path=<epic ledger>, cap_usd=250.0, reserve_usd=0.0)`. The prerequisite parameterizes `reserve()` with keyword-only `cap_usd` and `reserve_usd`, which is consistent. However the subject states reserve_usd=0 yields a $250 ceiling and that '$250 bounds actual finalized spend' via a post-finalize re-read and fatal halt. The prerequisite's reserve() gates only pre-flight estimate against cap minus reserve; it does not itself enforce a post-finalize cap re-check. The subject's post-finalize halt logic is subject-side, not prerequisite behavior, so this is compatible. The genuine inconsistency: the subject's estimate tier keys are `criteria-eval-cheap` and `criteria-eval-agent`, which the prerequisite adds — consistent. But the subject's acceptance ceiling of 250.0 relies on reserve_usd=0.0 giving a true $250 ceiling; the prerequisite's default reserve_usd is 30.0 and the boundary math is cap minus reserve. With reserve_usd=0.0 the ceiling is exactly cap_usd=250.0, which matches. This pairing is actually consistent on estimate keys and cap parameterization.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe16bd27634e91f1d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Budget enforcement","norm_id":"n749f891a8b